"""Human-readable conclusions keep research and current execution scope distinct."""
import json,pathlib
ROOT=pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parents[3];DEST=ROOT/'docs/research/continuous-income-20261114'
def write_report():
 s=json.loads((DEST/'summary.json').read_text());selected=next(r for r in s['management'] if r['scenario']==dict(risk=.4,trigger=2,trailATR=1,holdMinutes=1440));higher=next(r for r in s['management'] if r['scenario']==dict(risk=.5,trigger=2,trailATR=1,holdMinutes=1440));income=next(r for r in s['selectedIncome'] if r['scenario']['risk']==.4)
 lines=['# Continuous income and faster funding — 14 November 2026','','## Decision','','There is a stronger historical candidate: one Gold M15 RSI method, risk 0.4%, fixed initial 1.5 ATR/structure stop and 5R target, start trailing after 2R by ONE latest closed-bar ATR, maximum holding24h. Its six complete May–October months returned '+f"{selected['sixMonthNetPct']:.2f}% net, a geometric average of {selected['geometricAverageMonthlyPct']:.2f}% per month. Five of six months were positive; four reached at least2%. Worst full month {selected['worstFullMonth']:.2f}%, maximum observed equity drawdown through12November {selected['final']['drawdownPct']:.2f}%."+' This is a reused-history development selection, not dependable monthly income or provider qualification.','','This RSI trailing policy is NOT wired for customer execution. It remains outside the thirteen reviewed signal/demo configurations. The existing Gold compression configuration is wired, but its native account returns must not be substituted for its weaker canonical scanner review. No count of fourteen, new execution qualification or paid-live readiness is granted here.','','## Monthly returns, continued trading','','USD25,000 account; no profit cutoff, no monthly capital reset and no withdrawals. Marks include open-position P&L; monthly return uses preceding month-end equity. Real ordered reference bid/ask quotes, commissions, adverse fills, delayed entry/management and adverse financing are included. November ends12November and is partial.','','| Month | 0.4% risk, selected one-ATR trail | 0.5% risk, same management |','|---|---:|---:|']
 for a,b in zip(selected['monthly'],higher['monthly']):lines.append(f"| {a['month']}{' partial' if a['partial'] else ''} | {a['returnPct']:+.3f}% | {b['returnPct']:+.3f}% |")
 lines +=['',f"At0.5% risk the full six-month return was {higher['sixMonthNetPct']:.2f}%, geometric monthly average {higher['geometricAverageMonthlyPct']:.2f}%, and maximum drawdown {higher['final']['drawdownPct']:.2f}%. The 0.4% candidate offers a lower drawdown comparison; increasing risk is not assumed to improve reliability.",'','The selected-profile daily replay must reconcile exactly with the management study; publisher checks both ending marked equity and drawdown. Numerical loss rules are a buffered STATIC8% overall / daily4% reference. The native replay uses UTC daily reset; actual product static mode uses observed Europe/Prague tracking. This difference, actual firm terms, contracts, news policies and provider fills remain material limits.','','## 30–40-day funded windows','','These overlapping windows come from one continuously trading selected0.4% account; they are not independent fresh-account starts or payout requests. Missing follow-up is excluded and windows retain losing results.','','| Horizon | Observed windows | At least2% | At least3% | At least5% | Negative | Median | Worst |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
 for days,r in income['rolling'].items():lines.append(f"| {days} days | {r['windows']} | {r['atLeast2']} | {r['atLeast3']} | {r['atLeast5']} | {r['negative']} | {r['median']:.2f}% | {r['worst']:.2f}% |")
 lines +=['','## Additional cost sensitivity','','The source already includes adverse quote fills, commission and financing. These cases multiply all three modeled costs again, keeping the same3s entry delay and exact selected rule. They are not historical fee guarantees.','','| Risk | Cost multiple | Six full months | Maximum observed drawdown | Failed numerical guard |','|---|---|---:|---:|---|']
 for r in s['costStress']:
  lines.append(f"| {r['scenario']['risk']}% | {r['scenario']['costMultiplier']}x | {r['sixMonthNetPct']:+.2f}% | {r['final']['drawdownPct']:.2f}% | {r['final']['failed']} |")
 lines +=['','Neither a positive average nor majority-positive windows establishes2–3% every month. Do not advertise an account-equity mark as cash paid to a buyer.','','## Evaluation speed and risk sweet spot','','Thirteen overlapping starts, four genuine entry days per evaluation phase, modeled24h handoff; target8% or10%, verification5%. One-ATR trailing was selected after reused-period management tests. All counts retain partial starts and report censoring. No untouched holdout is claimed.','','| Selected trail | Evaluation risk | Targets | Funded within30days | Within40days | Censored at40days | Guard failures through follow-up |','|---|---:|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
 for r in s['challenges']:
  if r['model']!='Selected1ATR':continue
  a,b=r['horizons']['30'],r['horizons']['40'];lines.append(f"| 1ATR after2R | {r['risk']}% | {r['challengeTarget']}% /5% | {a['hits']}/{a['starts']} | {b['hits']}/{b['starts']} | {b['censored']} | {r['failedThroughAvailableFollowup']} |")
 lines +=['','The0.75% evaluation case is a middle-risk research comparison; the1% case is faster but had guard failures. Both exceed the UNCHANGED production Prop0.5% risk cap. These are not available customer acceleration presets. The0.5% version did not establish one-month or40-day funding. Failure counts cover available follow-up, not necessarily the same30/40-day horizon.','','## Scanner, arbitration and conditional entries','','Canonical BTC/ETH August2026 ablation, selected three reviewed4h configurations, USD500, risk0.5%, identical source and costs:','','| Mode | Authorized entries | Closed trades | Net marked return |','|---|---:|---:|---:|']
 for r in s['admission']:
  m=r['metrics'];lines.append(f"| {r['name']} | {m['authorizedEntries']} | {m['closedTrades']} | {m['netReturnPct']:+.3f}% |")
 lines +=['','Production and relaxed admission produced identical results here; loosening admission did not repair the weak entry outcomes. Conditional-only generated no trades for these selected immediate-entry definitions, so this sample says nothing about whether a different conditional setup should skip confirmation. The earlier Gold study did show admission sensitivity, retained in the preceding execution-frontier report. Do not generalize either experiment across every market.','','Native one-position comparisons also favor focus: adding USDJPY reduced results; combining RSI and compression generally increased drawdown. These tests merge actual quote timestamps and share ONE cash balance and at most one open position across permitted assets; they never sum independent account returns into a fictional portfolio. A complete two-simultaneous-position portfolio is not claimed.','','## Small personal capital, higher risk and leverage','','900 BTC/ETH cases use genuine vendor-checksummed USDT-perpetual5m data with July warmup and August–October trading. USD100/500 capitals, risks0.5/1/2/3/5%, leverage ceilings1/3/5/10/20, three fixed configurations, single assets/pair, baseline/1.5x costs. This is native OHLC research, not canonical scanner/provider certification; cross-margin maintenance is an explicit0.5% numerical approximation, not historical venue mark-price liquidation.','','For USD500, ETH-only4h trend pullback1.5ATR/5R, ceiling5, baseline costs:','','| Requested risk | Three-month return | Drawdown |','|---|---:|---:|']
 for risk in [.5,1,2,3,5]:
  r=next(r for r in s['crypto'] if r['symbols']==['ETHUSDT'] and r['config']['stopAtr']==1.5 and r['capital']==500 and r['risk']==risk and r['leverage']==5 and r['costMultiplier']==1);lines.append(f"| {risk}% | {r['netPct']:+.2f}% | {r['drawdownPct']:.2f}% |")
 lines+=['','BTC and the combined pair did not share that result. At5% risk, for example, BTC in the same comparison lost21.63% with32.58% drawdown. This supports asset selection and lower defaults, not high-risk promotion. Increasing leverage does not change P&L for a fixed position; it changes margin/capacity and can permit larger exposure.','','The M15 Gold model often could not place minimum-lot trades on USD100/500 at low risk. Fifty small-account M15 cases include ceilings5/10/20/50/100. Eighty additional genuine-quote M1/M5 short-holding cases did not repair the economics: many remained inactive or lost heavily. Zero entries are shown as inactivity, not capital-preservation success. Requested risk can be reduced by minimum lot, margin and remaining risk room. Personal stress loss guards deliberately differ from customer defaults.','','## What changed in the product code','','- New onboarding defaults to0.5% risk. Saved lower-risk preferences and existing assignments are retained; Prop still clamps to0.5%. No2–5% customer risk limits were raised.','- Funded objectives support2%,3%,5%; continued trading is the default. Optional close-and-pause remains. ACTIVE cycles adopt the approved behavior on their next valid snapshot; already-latched closures cannot be bypassed or silently restarted.','- FTMO two-step Swing setup can use its source-bound static initial-balance / Prague midnight daily-balance basis. Existing approved high-water profiles are not rewritten. Actual observed peaks and continuity remain stored. Account loss percentages, exposure, position protection, customer isolation and entry renewal remain enforced.','- Static context is checked against the CURRENT approved account source at evidence recording and authorization. Wrong program, source, clock and phase fail validation. Shared Brain version1.1.2 records the new basis behavior.','- Admin controls show the loss calculation and continue/stop choice. The funded panel distinguishes an informational objective from a latched payout cutoff.','','Code and migrations are prepared in the existing PR. No hosted migration, deployment, account activation, broker order, Telegram publication or payment action occurred. Browser UI verification is not claimed.','','## No-payout months clarified','','In the previous USD25,000 /0.4% /5%-cutoff recurring model, August had USD−451.55 closed trading net, September+131.06 and October+512.03. None completed the next payout threshold. The numerical guard was not breached, maximum observed drawdown6.85%; that is not a claim of full real-firm compliance. No payout did not mean zero trading profit.','','## Buyer economics','','At USD25,000,2% gross trading profit is USD500. With an illustrative80% customer split and USD100 software fee, that leaves USD300;3% leaves USD500. Those are arithmetic examples, not projected monthly payouts. At USD500 capital, a USD100 monthly fee alone requires20% profit just to cover the fee. Modest-return small personal accounts therefore need different pricing or service scope to deliver customer value.','','## Reproduction and evidence','','Acquire the eight crypto archives with scripts/research/acquire-canonical-history.py and vendor checksum verification; source manifests are embedded. Native quote ZIPs and decoded M1 rows remain outside git with exact hashes, row counts and observed boundaries. Existing execution-frontier source supplies causal closed-bar features. Run run.py, focused.py, selected_income.py, challenge.py, challenge_trail1.py, crypto.py, small_gold.py, management.py and admission.py from this folder. The studies overlap; their counts are not independent evidence. Earlier peak/static engine sources are archived so completed source identities remain reproducible. Publisher asserts account cash ledgers and selected-profile parity; SHA256SUMS.json covers every deliverable.','','Validation:151 operations TS tests,28 database tests,8 operations Python tests and4 native research tests (the latter cover shared cash, asset ownership, quote ordering and delayed stop fills); app typecheck,39 edge bundles and production build. Tests verify engineering/accounting correctness, not future profitability.','','Official references checked14November2026: [FTMO two-step objectives](https://ftmo.com/en/2-step-challenge/), [FTMO detailed static and daily rules](https://ftmo.com/en/trading-objectives/), [Bybit fixed-position leverage/P&L](https://www.bybit.com/en/help-center/article/Does-Leverage-Affects-Your-Unrealized-P-L). Reference broker data and explicit costs are not actual buyer fills.']
 (DEST/'RESULTS.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
if __name__=='__main__':write_report()
